course: dictionary
lesson: 9257
title: Sour: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. To know which one you need, look at what the word describes and at the words around it. Sour can describe food, milk, a person's mood, or something getting worse.
explain: «Lick a lemon and it is sour» means sour is a sharp taste, like a lemon or vinegar. «Milk left out on a warm table goes sour» shows that milk turns sour when it goes bad.
explain: In a story, «a sour face» shows someone is cross. As a verb, to sour means to become worse or less friendly. Check the clues: is it a taste, a food going bad, or a feeling?
fact: Sour is one of the basic tastes: sweet, sour, salty, bitter and savoury (umami).
fact: Sour tastes are caused by acids.
fact: «Milk left out on a warm table goes sour» because bacteria multiply fast in warmth and make acid; the fridge slows them down.
fact: Phrases you will meet include «sour cream», «sweet and sour» and «go sour».
exercise: «Lick a lemon and it is sour.» What does sour mean here? | A loud noise | A kind, friendly feeling | *A sharp taste, like a lemon | To grow taller
exercise: «A sour mood spoiled the picnic.» What does sour suggest? | Sweet and sticky | Happy and bouncy | *Bad-tempered and unfriendly | Very hot
exercise: «Milk left out on a warm table goes sour.» Why does the milk go sour? | It is poured into a cup | Because it is cold | *Bacteria multiply fast in warmth and make acid | It is put in a fridge
test: Which of these is one of the basic tastes? | *Salty | Quick | Tall | Loud
test: «Let them ferment under leaves for several days.» What does ferment mean here? | Cut into small pieces | *Slowly change, helped by tiny living things | Freeze in the cold | Ship across the sea
exam: In «A sour mood spoiled the picnic», what does sour mean? | *Bad-tempered and unfriendly | Very hot | A sharp taste | Gone bad like milk
